cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data, please cite the paper below (preferred-citation)."
type: dataset
title: "RepairOrReplace_LCE2027_results: Results and figures for 'To repair or replace? Consumer decision pathways and their influence on the environmental assessments of repairing'"
abstract: >-
  Results (lifespan factor / environmental break-even point) of 576 repair/replace
  combinations for a hand blender, a smartphone and a pair of jeans, based on Carbon
  Footprint and Material Footprint, together with the figures and the life cycle inventory
  of the sewing machine. The underlying footprints are not included because they are
  derived from ecoinvent; they are available from the corresponding author on request.
